{"from": "passage:mk-09-01", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mt-16-28-coming-in-kingdom"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-01", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-16-28", "note": "Mark adds that the Kingdom comes 'with power'."}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-02", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mt-17-01-high-mountain"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-02", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-17-01", "note": "Same event, 'after six days', up a high mountain; Mark says 'he was changed into another form in front of them'."}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-03", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mk-09-03-garments-white"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-04", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mt-17-03-moses-elijah-appear"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-04", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-17-03", "note": "Same event; Mark lists Elijah before Moses, Matthew Moses before Elijah."}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-05", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mt-17-04-three-tents"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-05", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-17-04", "note": "Same proposal of three tents; Mark has Peter address Jesus as 'Rabbi', Matthew as 'Lord', and Mark adds that the disciples were very afraid (9:6)."}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-07", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mk-09-07-cloud-voice"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-07", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-17-05", "note": "Same voice from the bright cloud; Mark's wording ends 'Listen to him', Matthew adds 'in whom I am well pleased'."}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-09", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mk-09-09-messianic-secret"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-09", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-17-09", "note": "Same command on coming down from the mountain."}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-11", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mt-17-10-13-elijah-first"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-12", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mt-17-10-13-elijah-first"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-13", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mt-17-10-13-elijah-first"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-13", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-17-12", "note": "Both say Elijah has come and was treated as they wished; Mark adds 'even as it is written about him', Matthew 'they did not recognize him'."}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-17", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mk-09-17-mute-deaf-spirit"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-20", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mk-09-17-mute-deaf-spirit"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-21", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mk-09-17-mute-deaf-spirit"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-22", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mk-09-17-mute-deaf-spirit"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-25", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mk-09-17-mute-deaf-spirit"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-29", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mk-09-29-prayer-fast"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-31", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mt-17-22-passion-prediction"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-31", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-17-22", "note": "The same passion prediction; Mark has Jesus 'passing through Galilee' and not wanting anyone to know it, Matthew 'staying in Galilee'."}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-33", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mt-18-01-greatest-in-kingdom"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-33", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-18-01", "note": "Same occasion at Capernaum; Mark: in the house, the disciples silent about their dispute; Matthew: 'in that hour' the disciples ask who is greatest."}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-34", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mt-18-01-greatest-in-kingdom"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-34", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-18-01", "note": "The dispute on the road about who was greatest parallels Matthew's question 'Who then is greatest in the Kingdom of Heaven?'."}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-35", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mt-18-01-greatest-in-kingdom"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-35", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mk-09-35-first-servant"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-35", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-18-04", "note": "Matthew: 'whoever humbles himself as this little child... is the greatest'; Mark: 'last of all, and servant of all'."}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-36", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mt-18-01-greatest-in-kingdom"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-36", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-18-02", "note": "The little child set among them; Mark adds that he took the child in his arms."}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-37", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-18-05", "note": "Receiving one such little child in his name = receiving Jesus and the one who sent him."}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-38", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mk-09-38-exorcist"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-41", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mt-10-42-cup-cold-water"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-41", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-10-42", "note": "The cup-of-water saying; Mark: 'a cup of water to drink in my name... he will in no way lose his reward'; Matthew: 'a cup of cold water' to one of these little ones."}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-42", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mt-18-06-millstone-drowning"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-42", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-18-06", "note": "The same millstone saying in a different discourse setting; Mark: 'thrown into the sea', Matthew: 'sunk in the depths of the sea'."}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-43", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mt-18-08-09-cut-off-gehenna"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-43", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-18-08", "note": "Cut off the hand rather than be cast into Gehenna; Mark names only the hand here and adds 'the unquenchable fire', Matthew has hand or foot and 'the eternal fire'."}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-44", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mk-09-48-worm-isaiah-66-24"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-45", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mt-18-08-09-cut-off-gehenna"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-46", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mk-09-48-worm-isaiah-66-24"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-47", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mt-18-08-09-cut-off-gehenna"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-47", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-18-09", "note": "Pluck out the eye rather than be cast into the Gehenna of fire; Mark: enter 'God's Kingdom' with one eye, Matthew 'into life'."}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-48", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mk-09-48-worm-isaiah-66-24"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-49", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mk-09-49-salted-with-fire"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-50", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:mt-05-13-salt"}
{"from": "passage:mk-09-50", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-05-13", "note": "'Salt is good, but if the salt has lost its saltiness' parallels the Sermon on the Mount saying; Mark adds 'have salt in yourselves, and be at peace with one another'."}
{"from": "artifact:great-isaiah-scroll", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-09-48-worm-isaiah-66-24", "grade": "B", "note": "The Great Isaiah Scroll (ca. 125 BCE) carries Isaiah 66:24, the verse Mark quotes, within the oldest known complete copy of the Book of Isaiah - grade B under the binding Isaiah rule for quotation claims. It says nothing about Mark's use of the verse."}
{"from": "text:targum-jonathan-isaiah-66-24", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-09-48-worm-isaiah-66-24", "grade": "C", "note": "Targum Jonathan interprets Isaiah 66:24 as the evildoers judged in Gehenna - the worm-and-fire motif in Jewish interpretation of the verse. The Targum's final form is later than the 1st century, so it may not describe 30s CE usage exactly."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-8-eleazar", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-09-17-mute-deaf-spirit", "grade": "C", "note": "Josephus saw Eleazar 'releasing people that were demoniacal' before Vespasian - Jewish demon-expulsion was a living 1st-century practice. It attests the practice, not this healing."}
{"from": "text:hippocrates-sacred-disease", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-09-17-mute-deaf-spirit", "grade": "C", "note": "The Hippocratic treatise treats the 'sacred disease' - convulsions and foaming - as a natural illness known to Greek medicine; the symptom picture was a recognized condition. It says nothing about the exorcism."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-8-eleazar", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-09-38-exorcist", "grade": "C", "note": "Jewish practitioners cast out demons in the 1st century (Eleazar before Vespasian, Josephus Ant. 8.46-49); a non-follower doing so in Jesus's name is the kind of practice this attests. It attests the practice, not this episode."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-3-sacrifices", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-09-49-salted-with-fire", "grade": "C", "note": "Josephus, on the manner of sacrifices: after slaying, the priests 'divide them into parts, and salt them with salt, and lay them upon the altar' - salting belonged to sacrificial practice."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-3-sacrifices", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikisource-ant3-sacrifices"}
{"from": "text:isaiah-66-24", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:bible-api-isaiah-66-24"}
