{"from": "artifact:papyrus-45", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-papyrus-45-contents"}
{"from": "text:isaiah-66-24", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mk-09-48-worm-isaiah-66-24", "note": "Isaiah 66:24 (WEB): 'their worm will not die, nor will their fire be quenched' - the verse Mark quotes as a refrain. A biblical cross-reference, not independent evidence."}
{"from": "text:leviticus-2-13", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mk-09-49-salted-with-fire", "note": "Leviticus 2:13 (WEB): 'With all your offerings you shall offer salt' - the sacrificial salt rule behind Mark's saying. A biblical cross-reference, not independent evidence."}
{"from": "claim:mk-09-17-mute-deaf-spirit", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-17-15-moonstruck-boy", "note": "Same exorcism; Mark describes a mute and deaf spirit with symptoms from childhood, Matthew 17:15 a 'moonstruck' (seleniazetai) boy who often falls into fire and water."}
{"from": "claim:mk-09-35-first-servant", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-20-25-rulers-lord-it-over", "note": "Mark gives the 'first = servant of all' saying at Capernaum (9:35); Matthew has it on the way up to Jerusalem (20:26-27), in the same discourse as the rulers-lording saying. A difference of setting between Gospels, not evidence."}
